 "text": "Hi! How's life treating you? Of course. Do you want start with pasta and make sure the sauce isn't touched, or go with rice and pick one dish that's completely gluten free? Read the ingredients, look for things with wheat or barley in them, or ask the label. Bread, pasta, some pastry, and beer. Also some processed meats and some canned goods. You could make soy soy sauce instead, or get a lupin sauce, or just use lots of ginger and soy. It's really not. There's actually a lot you can eat. A lot of restaurants list their gluten free dishes.",
